<svg viewBox="0 0 720 420" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The golden data trio: quality, coverage, quantity">
  <text x="360" y="30" font-size="14" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">If training is cooking, data is the ingredients — three things must be right</text>

  <!-- quality -->
  <rect x="40" y="52" width="205" height="250" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="142" y="80" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Quality</text>
  <text x="142" y="98" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-faint)">are the ingredients fresh?</text>
  <text x="54" y="122" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">six characteristics:</text>
  <text x="54" y="142" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· relevant to the task</text>
  <text x="54" y="160" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· aligned with requirements</text>
  <text x="62" y="176" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-faint)">(“aligned”, not just “accurate”)</text>
  <text x="54" y="194" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· consistent across annotators</text>
  <text x="54" y="212" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· correctly formatted</text>
  <text x="54" y="230" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· sufficiently unique</text>
  <text x="54" y="248" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· compliant with policies</text>
  <text x="54" y="276" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">1K curated examples can beat</text>
  <text x="54" y="291" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">hundreds of thousands of noisy ones</text>

  <!-- coverage -->
  <rect x="258" y="52" width="205" height="250" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="360" y="80" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Coverage</text>
  <text x="360" y="98" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-faint)">the right mix of ingredients?</text>
  <text x="272" y="122" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">match real usage diversity:</text>
  <text x="272" y="142" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· long AND short instructions</text>
  <text x="272" y="160" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· typos if users make typos</text>
  <text x="272" y="178" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· topics, formats, languages,</text>
  <text x="280" y="194" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">turn counts your app needs</text>
  <text x="272" y="218" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· dimensions differ per app —</text>
  <text x="280" y="234" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">translation ≠ global chatbot</text>
  <text x="272" y="276" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">high-quality + diverse beats</text>
  <text x="272" y="291" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">either alone (same data size)</text>

  <!-- quantity -->
  <rect x="476" y="52" width="205" height="250" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="578" y="80" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Quantity</text>
  <text x="578" y="98" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-faint)">how much do you need?</text>
  <text x="490" y="122" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">depends on:</text>
  <text x="490" y="142" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· method: full FT wants 1000s+,</text>
  <text x="498" y="158" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">PEFT shines on hundreds</text>
  <text x="490" y="176" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· task complexity</text>
  <text x="490" y="194" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· base model strength (stronger</text>
  <text x="498" y="210" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">base → fewer examples)</text>
  <text x="490" y="234" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">· returns diminish — plot the</text>
  <text x="498" y="250" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">25%/50%/100% gain curve</text>
  <text x="490" y="276" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">start with ~50 examples: visible</text>
  <text x="490" y="291" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent-ink)">gains predict more from more data</text>

  <rect x="40" y="322" width="640" height="64" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
  <text x="58" y="346" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Bootstrap when high-quality data is scarce:</text>
  <text x="58" y="366" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">self-supervised on raw domain docs → supervised pairs · less-relevant data (tweets) → relevant data (reviews) · synthetic → real</text>

  <text x="360" y="410" font-size="12" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">Best data source of all: your own application — a data flywheel matches your distribution perfectly.</text>
</svg>
